# Sunnah Al-Hadi

A mobile application for reminding users of daily Sunnah practices, designed to gently notify and guide through beautiful Islamic reminders.

---

## What is Sunnah Al-Hadi?

**Sunnah Al-Hadi** is an Android application built using Jetpack Compose that helps Muslims implement Sunnah practices in their daily lives. The app sends daily notifications with short reminders about Sunnah acts, making it easy to learn and incorporate them into your routine.

### **Key Features**

- Receive daily Sunnah reminders via push notifications.
- Clean, modern UI using Jetpack Compose.
- Notification permission management (Android 13+).
- Elegant rationale dialogs if permissions are denied/blocked.
- Simple navigation to app settings for permissions.
- Expandable for additional Islamic reminders and features.

---

## ⚙️ How Does It Work?

Sunnah Al-Hadi requests notification permissions (Android 13+), and after obtaining consent, sends out daily notifications.

### **Notification Permission Flow**

- On first app launch or when required, asks for notification permissions.
- If denied, explains why the permission is needed.
- If user selects "Don't ask again," suggests enabling notifications via app settings.

**Key File:** 
`app/src/main/java/com/ryen/sunnah_alhadi/presentation/NotifcationPermissionHandler.kt` 
This composable manages the permission request flow and rationale dialogs.

### **Architecture Overview**

- **UI Layer:** Jetpack Compose screens and dialogs.
- **Permission Utils:** Helper for checking system notification permission status.
- **Notification Manager:** (presumed elsewhere) Schedules and pushes Sunnah reminders.
- **Navigation:** (if present) Handles screen transitions.

---

## ️ Project Structure

```plaintext
/app
 └─ /src/main/java/com/ryen/sunnah_alhadi/
 ├─ presentation/
 │ └─ NotifcationPermissionHandler.kt # Permission UI logic
 └─ util/
 └─ NotificationPermissionUtils.kt # Helpers for notification permissions
```
> _Other directories/files exist for settings, notifications scheduling, etc._

---

## Usage

1. **Build the app** in Android Studio or via `./gradlew assembleDebug`.
2. **Install on your device**.
3. **Run** – on first launch, grant notification permissions.
4. Receive daily Sunnah notifications!

---

## Contributing

- **Fork/clone**, create a new branch, and submit pull requests.
- Keep code clean and document public functions.
- Please write tests if creating logic-heavy features.

---

## ✅ Completed

- [x] Notification permission flow for Android 13+ (TIRAMISU)
- [x] Permission rationale dialog
- [x] Open app settings deep link for blocked permissions
- [x] Basic UI using Material 3/Jetpack Compose

## In Process

- [ ] Expand Sunnah content source
- [ ] Enhance notification scheduling (custom times, quiet hours)
- [ ] Add translations/localization
- [ ] Improve onboarding UI/UX

## Todo

- [ ] Add in-app settings to customize notification timing
- [ ] Implement advanced notification options (sound, vibration, etc.)
- [ ] Add daily/weekly challenge tracking
- [ ] Integrate learning modules for Sunnah practices
- [ ] Unit and UI tests
- [ ] Submit to Google Play Store

---

## License

[MIT License](LICENSE) (or the project’s actual license)

---

**Contact:** 
For suggestions, bugs, or feature requests, please open a GitHub issue or contact the maintainer.

